    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d354">

                <pb facs="0336" n="329" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg329"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.3394/265: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-05T13:00:00-04:00">August 5, 1937—1 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>139. Reference, your 221, July 22, 5 p.m., and previous.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>For your information. Commander-in-Chief<anchor n="48" xml:id="d354-f1"/>
                        recommends through the Navy Department that in view of the situation in Far
                        East this Department notify Japanese Government that proposed visit of the
                        Commander-in-Chief to Japan be indefinitely postponed. Both Departments
                        approve.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Please appropriately inform Foreign Office that visit will be indefinitely
                        postponed.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d354-f1" n="48" xml:id="d354-f1-content">
                <p>Admiral Harry E. Yarnell, Commander in Chief, U. S. Asiatic Fleet, at
                    Shanghai.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
